<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African Feb trade deficit 451.6 mln rand.</title>
<headline>S.African Feb trade deficit 451.6 mln rand.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa recorded a trade deficit of 451.6 million rand in February from a 517 million rand surplus in January, latest South African Revenue Service figures show.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists called for a 1.04 billion rand surplus from a range of 500 million to 1.5 billion rand.  </p>
<p>	  (Data in billions of rand - rounded)</p>
<p>			  Feb '97	     Jan '97	    Feb '96</p>
<p>Exports		  8.831		11.249		8.996</p>
<p>Imports		  9.283		10.732		7.726</p>
<p>Balance		 -0.452		 0.517		1.270</p>
<p>Cumulative totals:  Jan-Feb '97	 Jan-Feb '96</p>
<p>Exports		 20.081		16.385</p>
<p>Imports		 20.015		16.057</p>
<p>Balance		  0.066		 1.270</p>
<p>NOTE - This data covers the total foreign trade statistics of the common customs area of South Africa, Botswana, Lesotho, Namibia and Swaziland.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom (+27 11 482-1003)</p>
</text>
